From 90db1e9c84da202e3cce0d457ea7c732ab2e16ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hongtao <hongtao_zhang@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:13:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] octeon_ep: fail fast on control mailbox requests after
 heartbeat loss

send_mbox_req() waits up to 8 s for the firmware's reply. Once the
heartbeat is lost (the card rebooted or its control-plane agent died),
octep_hb_timeout_task() turns the carrier off and no reply will come,
yet every request still waits the full timeout. Several callers hold
RTNL while they wait: ethtool get_link_ksettings (and with it the sysfs
speed and duplex files), ethtool -S, MTU and MAC changes. Daemons that
poll /sys/class/net/*/speed then keep RTNL busy back to back, and every
other RTNL user on the host (RTM_GETLINK dumps such as getifaddrs() and
ip link, IPv6 addrconf work) stalls for seconds at a time.

Return -ENODEV right away while the heartbeat miss count is at or above
the configured limit. A heartbeat resets the count, so requests go
through again if the firmware comes back.
---
 drivers/octeon_ep/octep_ctrl_net.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/octeon_ep/octep_ctrl_net.c b/drivers/octeon_ep/octep_ctrl_net.c
index 1ae55d4..4d293db 100644
--- a/drivers/octeon_ep/octep_ctrl_net.c
+++ b/drivers/octeon_ep/octep_ctrl_net.c
@@ -48,6 +48,15 @@ static int send_mbox_req(struct octep_device *oct,
 {
 	int err, ret, cmd;
 
+	/* Firmware heartbeat lost (octep_hb_timeout_task turned the carrier
+	 * off): nobody will answer. Callers such as ethtool and the sysfs
+	 * speed/duplex files hold RTNL while they wait, so fail now instead
+	 * of stalling every RTNL user for the full timeout per request.
+	 */
+	if (oct->conf->fw_info.hb_miss_count &&
+	    atomic_read(&oct->hb_miss_cnt) >= oct->conf->fw_info.hb_miss_count)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	/* check if firmware is compatible for this request */
 	cmd = d->data.req.hdr.s.cmd;
 	if (octep_ctrl_net_h2f_cmd_versions[cmd] > oct->ctrl_mbox.max_fw_version ||
-- 
2.55.0

